0 -14 Td
(- Duplicate requests with the same Idempotency-Key) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Same Idempotency-Key with different payload \(conflict\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Retryable failures with controlled retries) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Non-retryable failures without retry) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Cancellation while processing) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Concurrency and race conditions) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Slow processing and long-running jobs) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -14 Td
(HTTP responses you will see) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- 202 Accepted: request saved and queued) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- 200 OK: request completed or already known) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- 400 Bad Request: missing or invalid input) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- 409 Conflict: same idempotency key used with different payload) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- 500 Internal Server Error: unexpected server issue) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -14 Td
(Principles we followed) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- SOLID: clear responsibilities for controller, service, job, and processor) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- ACID: database constraints and row locks keep data safe) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- DRY: shared logic for hashing and serialization) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- COC: standard Rails structure) Tj
0 -14 Td
0 -14 Td
(How it helps in real life) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- You never process the same request twice.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Users can safely retry calls without creating duplicates.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- The system keeps working even if parts fail temporarily.) Tj
0 -14 Td
